{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/592043-gifts-that-grant-extra-forms","id":592043,"title":"Gifts That Grant Extra Forms","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-15T16:51:22-07:00","id":592043,"title":"Gifts That Grant Extra Forms","content":"The more I dwell on Gifts like Rat-Thing, the more I wonder why some Fera didn't just have a basic adjustment made to their number of forms as a matter of course. It's not like it hasn't happened before, either; Rokea didn't have five forms until second edition, after all. Also, given the nature of character sheets, it seems like it might be a tad bothersome to have to go in and make a place to pencil in an extra form or two. Ditto with the notation form Attributes in alternate forms, since the numbers and slashes can get ambiguous with just a casual glance down at the format of stat notation for NPCs used in Werewolf, e.g. Strength 4 (6/8/7/5). It also seems like it would have been easier, and possibly more fun, not to wall basic forms behind a Rank requirement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T17:21:08-07:00","id":592111,"title":"","content":"Eh. I figure that's what Mixed-Morph perk is for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T17:56:58-07:00","id":592151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/592043-gifts-that-grant-extra-forms?p=592111#post592111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. I figure that's what Mixed-Morph perk is for.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's for mixing and matching what you already have, not providing discrete equivalents to Glabro and/or Hispo.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T19:06:37-07:00","id":592208,"title":"","content":"So I'm not sure what the question here is.<br /> Saur Ops, are you just wondering why all Fera do not have 5 forms?<br /> I think some Glabro-equivalent forms might be kind of useless. Corax come to mind.<br /> <br /> I actually like some Fera having only 3 forms. System-wise, it's easier for them to switch between the forms without spending Rage, since they need less successes. Needing 2 less successes to get from Homid to animal form does count for something.<br /> <br /> The Mokole having only 3 forms makes a bit of sense, given how their battle form comes about, though they are fairly unique in that sense.<br /> I liked 2 out of 3 of the Ratkin form Gifts. I think they can add a lot of flavor to the form spread. The Itchy-form gift though was very dumb, and something I've never included in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T19:49:27-07:00","id":592231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/592043-gifts-that-grant-extra-forms?p=592208#post592208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I'm not sure what the question here is.<br /> Saur Ops, are you just wondering why all Fera do not have 5 forms?<br /> I think some Glabro-equivalent forms might be kind of useless. Corax come to mind.<br /> <br /> I actually like some Fera having only 3 forms. System-wise, it's easier for them to switch between the forms without spending Rage, since they need less successes. Needing 2 less successes to get from Homid to animal form does count for something.<br /> <br /> The Mokole having only 3 forms mtakes a bit of sense, given how their battle form comes about, though they are fairly unique in that sense.<br /> I liked 2 out of 3 of the Ratkin form Gifts. I think they can add a lot of flavor to the form spread. The Itchy-form gift though was very dumb, and something I've never included in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No. I'm wondering why there are Gifts to grant extra forms in W20, instead of just having them be a normal part of any given Fera. It seems a pointless hassle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T03:07:13-07:00","id":592463,"title":"","content":"Particularly in the case of the Ratkin, I like the extra-forms-as-gifts thing as it helps differentiate the Ratkin breeds. It's a pity, though, that they left out the Rodens special form along with the general wacky tone of the kind...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}